No, I haven't. Not at all. The status line shows Dlvl:n where n decreases
by one as you enter Sokoban and every time you climb the stairs.

botl.c does this;

                Sprintf(buf, "Dlvl:%-2d ", depth(&u.uz));

so I think it's pretty clear that depth() decreases as you proceed through
Sokoban.

I'm not sure where you would "notice" that Sokoban was either 1 to 4 or -1
to -4. Such numbers are never presented to the player; only the Quest has
a shim to present it as numbers from 1 upwards. Evidently the internal
representation is -1 to -4. I hope you're not just trusting the fact that
spoilers have picked the convenient 1-4 representation.

Note also that in dungeon.c prev_level(), which is called by doup() in
do.c, simply does;

newlevel.dlevel = u.uz.dlevel - 1;

when not going into a branch.
